sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-santomea-turing-wavelength-s0> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-santomea-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-santomea-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Drosophila santomea Schnakenberg wavelength at 2.326 µm (Holocene, 0 Ma), pass 1 — MorphoEval overall 76.3/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 1 locks Schnakenberg parameters (a=0.130, b=0.870, Du=1, Dv=40) so the continuous critical wavelength is 2.326 µm at γ=1, age 0 Ma. Numeric growth rates match the analytic dispersion (Pearson r rounds to 1.0 at six decimals, RMSE 4.9e-5). The 12-frame 800×600 GIF and the comparison figure were written. The γ sweep, equal-diffusion ablation, scale-bar segmentation, and KS distances are listed as remediation_pending in pass1_metrics.json. Overall 76.3/100 (faithfulness 73.0, reproducibility 84.1); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 86, Morphological realism / specimen match 68, Parameter expressivity 64, Morphometric validation 70, Source and data traceability 86, Code-to-model traceability 82, Reproducibility package 84. Output judged: docs/media/drosophila_santomea_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-santomea-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d, image/png, 506876 B, 1248×960 px, artifact_sha256 c0f9011955e25636bbf84acbbdb74e4fe2c036ce9049b3d29716c09b56a4cec5 (sha256 c0f9011955e25636bbf84acbbdb74e4fe2c036ce9049b3d29716c09b56a4cec5), spec_fingerprint 6dd554cc130d1b0176b37753cfbd7be017befc53ffb878bd36cf5f79710bf34c. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 6dd554cc130d1b0176b37753cfbd7be017befc53ffb878bd36cf5f79710bf34c; artifact_sha256: c0f9011955e25636bbf84acbbdb74e4fe2c036ce9049b3d29716c09b56a4cec5; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/drosophila_santomea_turing_wavelength_s0/drosophila_santomea_specimen.jpg=9ea05ad5963c10d3..., datasets/drosophila_santomea_turing_wavelength_s0/drosophila_santomea_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=f16b54dd44acea38..., datasets/drosophila_santomea_turing_wavelength_s0/paper_citations.bib=fb23a9fc5fb610db...}. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952 gives k_c from the linearized reaction-diffusion Jacobian. | Jeong et al. 2008 show loss of abdominal tan expression in D. santomea. | Lachaise et al. 2000 described the species; Llopart et al. 2002 mapped the yakuba pigmentation difference.; reconstructed_in_script: Spatial unit ξ is chosen so γ = 1 yields λ_c = 2.326 µm. | Pass 1 integrates eigenvector-initialized modes and compares growth rates to σ(k).; transfer_boundary: Chronoseries neighbors are scored at this 2.3 µm tier only. Their primordium-slot parameters are not reused.; does_not_claim: That the source papers measured a 2.3 µm wavelength. | That the gallery spiral is a 2.3 µm micrograph. | That pass 1 already contains the γ sweep, ablation, scale bar, or KS test.." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Report a KS distance and keep RMSE next to Pearson r.",
            "remediation needed: Run the equal-diffusion ablation and record that σ(k_c) changes sign.",
            "remediation needed: Run the γ sweep and test that analytic wavelength falls as γ rises.",
            "remediation needed: Segment the gallery 100 µm scale bar and compare arm spacing with 2.326 µm." ;
        pk:hasScore "0.763"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 (single builder-assessor; no separate second-model pass)" ;
        dct:identifier "grok-4.7" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://github.com/fractastical> .
}

